drug therapy and so on. That's where the vast majority of investments are really going.

16
00:02:04,260 --> 00:02:12,880
But I would contend that this is not an individual problem. This is a societal issue and the roots of

17
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:22,460
this decline are in the socio-commercial technological landscape in which we have been soaking in for the

18
00:02:22,460 --> 00:02:29,180
last maybe five or six decades. There are two aspects that I would like to draw attention to.

19
00:02:29,180 --> 00:02:36,520
The first is a rise in individualism and this phenomenon which has been on for perhaps the last

20
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:43,980
five, six or seven decades has been about smaller family structures, people moving away from their

21
00:02:43,980 --> 00:02:52,320
roots and going to bigger cities coupled with a rise in focus on material comfort and performance

22
00:02:52,320 --> 00:03:00,940
orientation even within families and perhaps that rise in individualism may have something to do with

23
00:03:00,940 --> 00:03:10,160
this. And the second aspect is our relationship with technology. The smartphones have landed the world in the

24
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:18,560
palms of our hands and they have given us the possibility to ostensibly connect to anyone around the globe by merely pressing a button.

25
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:30,800
But on the other hand, it has taken us away from in-person societal connections and promoted a more sedentary lifestyle, thus

26
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:46,560
even further creating separation. So what might we do? Perhaps go back and examine our relationships with each other and what might we do to bring greater cohesion because human beings are inherently relational in nature.

27
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:58,560
And second, what might we do to re-examine our relationship with technology specifically our phones and perhaps prioritize human beings over that?

28
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:12,560
If you're a parent, I would say talk rather than text, hug over judge, listen rather than advice, bring love back into the center of your relationship at home.

29
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:28,540
Do not encourage an early relationship with smartphones. As institutions, organizations, schools, colleges, businesses, get intentional about community, gather locally and often bring to the

